elitebook-thermal-profile (1.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The GNOME indicator switches profiles over D-Bus through a new front end,
    elitebook-thermal-profile-dbus, and polkit lets the active local session
    do it without a password. The front end is started on demand, holds no
    capabilities and writes no setting: it forwards each authorized request
    to the daemon's control socket, which stays the only way in. When it is
    missing or fails, the indicator falls back to pkexec as before.
  * Ship the D-Bus policy, activation file and polkit action, and stop the
    front end when the package is removed.
  * Recommend python3-gi and polkitd; the GNOME indicator depends on
    python3-gi.
  * Point Secure Boot users at the new ryzen-smu-dkms package.

 -- Matteo Passeri <matteopasseri407@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200

elitebook-thermal-profile (1.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Replace the oneshot dispatcher, the udev rule, the sleep hook, the idle
    watcher and the Steam watcher with one daemon that is the only writer of
    power settings. It reconciles to a target and writes only what changed,
    rewrites everything hourly and after a resume, and rereads profiles.conf
    on its own. Profile commands reach it over a root-only socket.
  * Battery level updates no longer reapply the profile every minute, so the
    thermal record keeps building on battery and the idle overlay is no longer
    briefly overridden.
  * Add RUNTIME_PM and PANEL_POWER_SAVINGS profile keys: on battery, idle PCI
    devices may power down and the panel uses amdgpu power saving.
  * New commands: reassert, daemon, apply-once. status shows the idle stage.
  * AC and battery are reread on kernel power events instead of every second.
  * A profile without a VRM limit restores the firmware value, so the battery
    profile's 45 A limit no longer stays in force on AC until reboot.
  * battery-saver holds until the battery climbs 2 points above the
    threshold, so capacity jitter no longer flips profiles.
  * Upgrades from earlier packages disable the old watcher units and restart
    the service, which is now a long-running daemon.
  * On battery the VRM peak current limit holds every profile, including a
    manual choice and a Steam game.
  * The service stops retrying on configuration errors (exit 78) and after
    10 crashes in 10 minutes.
  * GNOME indicator: declares GNOME Shell 51 and shows when the service is
    not running.
  * The CPU policy is read back every 30 s and rewritten if it drifted; a
    cpufreq driver stuck at the nominal clock is re-registered (at most
    hourly). amd-pstate dynamic EPP is turned off where present.
  * Deep idle no longer toggles boost: its 1.8 GHz cap already keeps boost
    out.

 -- Matteo Passeri <matteopasseri407@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 12 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200

elitebook-thermal-profile (0.9.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Protect against battery brownouts and transient voltage droops under heavy
    multi-core/AVX2 load: set battery profile burst power (FAST) to 22W,
    Tctl thermal target to 80 °C, and apply a 45A VRM peak current (EDC) limit
    via RyzenAdj (--vrmmax-current).
  * Add --vrmmax-current support to SMU limit application with profiles.conf
    overrides for VRMMAX_MA (15-120A).
  * Support BOOST and MAX_FREQ_KHZ overrides in profiles.conf.
  * Persist and report VRM max current in status and status --json.

 -- Matteo Passeri <matteopasseri407@users.noreply.github.com>  Wed, 07 Oct 2026 19:35:00 +0200

elitebook-thermal-profile (0.8.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Rewrite the dispatcher from bash to stdlib-only Python with identical
    CLI, state files and messages; add status --json for scripts.
  * Skip sysfs writes when the value is already in force; SMU limits are
    still reapplied every run so firmware resets keep healing.
  * Share sysfs helpers and CPU policy application among dispatcher,
    watchers and guard in one module.
  * Rewrite the update guard and the hibernate preflight from bash to
    Python as well; the hibernate config is parsed instead of sourced as
    root shell, and the system-sleep hook now runs Python too.
  * Name the config file line in refused profile override warnings.

 -- Matteo Passeri <matteopasseri407@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 08 Sep 2026 17:23:00 +0200

